{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1ikDAuFrXdEXf2LqRg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0156nNt5Ae9qmigUxt4apZ6H","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 568,580p AI_GUIDE.md; echo; grep -n \"Shell\\b\\|class Shell\\|_settingsRows\\|glyphs: {\\|const G57 =\\|GLYPHS =\\|_hat(\\|st === 'helmet'\\|if (this.voice && Math.floor\\|menu(name\\|_drawHD(\" my-3d2dge.js | head -40","description":"Read Sports recipe and locate engine change points"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":237,"cache_read_input_tokens":225499,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":237},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1931e3d-b97b-4f9d-8b9d-c7660f7740b5","uuid":"50e8376d-3932-40e9-84e9-9ebabba4ea99","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:03:43.589Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1ijnsa3qT2mMrAYrPD","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0156nNt5Ae9qmigUxt4apZ6H":{"command":"sed -n 568,580p AI_GUIDE.md; echo; grep -n \"Shell\\b\\|class Shell\\|_settingsRows\\|glyphs: {\\|const G57 =\\|GLYPHS =\\|_hat(\\|st === 'helmet'\\|if (this.voice && Math.floor\\|menu(name\\|_drawHD(\" my-3d2dge.js | head -40","description":"Read Sports recipe and locate engine change points"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0156nNt5Ae9qmigUxt4apZ6H","type":"tool_result","content":"**Sports (Sensible Soccer, NBA Jam, Tecmo Bowl).** Start from the SPORTS slice: two against two in a walled cage, up to four players.\n- The field is a `TileMap` cage in `threequarter` (boards that cut low before the camera, nets); the ball and the players are `E.Body`s. The ball bounces off the ground and the boards (`bounce`), and curls: turn its velocity a little across its path each step while the shooter pushes sideways (aftertouch).\n- A pass leads the teammate (aim where it is going, not where it is); a lob over a defender is `E.arc(from, to, gravity, { apex })`, the throw that lands at its feet; a shot's power fills a meter while its button is held and goes on letting go.\n- The players a person doesn't run play by formation, by where the ball is: with it, the other one runs ahead on the far side; without it, the nearer presses and the other covers the goal. `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })` lets players 2 to 4 in, each taking a side's next player.\n\n**First-person dungeon (Wizardry, Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder).** The 3D CRAWLER kit (the grid module). The 3D engine's `'fixed'` camera at the party's eyes over a level of 2 x 2 tiles a cell; each step and quarter turn is a tween, so the view glides. Gates are `world.thing('door')`s that rise (`world.unlock` for one with a key); the monsters walk an `E.Grid` cell to cell; `E.Fog` keeps what the party has seen for the automap; `E.Turns` in `'atb'` is real time (Dungeon Master), in `'speed'` the dungeon waits for the party (Wizardry). The party's portraits sit under the view (`rig.drawPortrait`).\n\n**Twin-stick shooter (Robotron 2084, Smash TV).** Start from the ADVENTURE kit (a `Body` hero in rooms) with the SHOOTER's ships and bullets.\n- One fixed room in `topdown` (`res: [320, 240]`, `expand`): the hero a `Body` moved by `input.move()`, the left stick or WASD; it fires the way the right stick points (`input.padAim`), else toward the mouse (`input.pointer()` to a ground point), else the way it moves, a shot every 0.08 s from an `E.Bullets` pool (`plane: 'ground'`).\n- Waves spawn from the room's edges by a timeline; grunts walk straight at the hero, others wander, hulks can't be killed, humans to rescue for points. `cam.shake` and `game.freeze(.03)` on every kill keep it loud; `E.Arcade` keeps the score, the lives and the table.\n\n**Bomberman.** Start from the PUZZLE slice's grid or the ARCADE's maze (the grid module).\n- The arena is an `E.Grid` of hard blocks on even cells and soft blocks to break; players and foes are `E.GridMover`s (a turn asked early is kept).\n\n41: *    interface (title, pause, settings, help, results, map screens and a HUD with a minimap) from data: new E.Shell(game,\n1263:const PAD_GLYPHS = {\n1304:const GLYPHS = {\n1322:const G57 = {\n2357:    /** the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null */\n2500:  menu(name) {\n2530:    if (this.o.menu !== false) new Shell(this, { system: true });\n2973: *    E.Shell draws the menu's screens (pause, settings, controls): section 21d.\n2999:  glyphs: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['xbox', 'Xbox'], ['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['nintendo', 'Nintendo'], ['generic', 'Positions']], apply: (g, v) => { g.input.glyphs = v; } },\n3031:    /** onChange(key, value): called after every change (E.Shell's settings.onChange goes through it) */\n3877:  /** open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or\n4347:    if (this.o.style === 'classic') this._drawClassic(g, ox, oy, view); else this._drawHD(g, ox, oy, view);\n4353:  _drawHD(g, ox, oy, view) {\n4479:        if (o.hat) this._hat(g, Sp, J, r, H);\n4501:      if (o.hat) this._hat(g, Sp, J, r, H);\n4604:        if (o.hat) this._hat(g, Sp, J, r, H);\n4637:  _hat(g, Sp, J, r, H) {\n4645:    } else if (st === 'helmet') {  // robot / knight helmet that leaves the face open\n8956:    if (this.voice && Math.floor(this.shown) > prev && (this._blip++ % 2 === 0)) this.game.audio.sfx(this.voice);\n9091: *      const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: { accent: '#d9b77c' }, settings: { items: ['sound', 'volume', 'motion'] },\n9103: *    THE STANDARD MENU: every game gets one (new E.Game makes this shell for itself, and a game's own E.Shell takes over\n9109: *    false }, quit: 'title' } }) adjusts it; menu: false, or new E.Shell(game, { standard: false }), leaves it out.\n9163:class Shell {\n9165:   * new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings',\n9373:  _settingsRows(add) {\n9460:    if (name === 'settings') this._settingsRows(add);\n9585:E.Shell = Shell;\n13389:  /** the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save\n14126:- rts.fog (E.Fog: the player's sight; walls block it), rts.visible(u); rts.minimap() is E.Shell's hud({ minimap }) (the\n14399:  /** E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera */","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1931e3d-b97b-4f9d-8b9d-c7660f7740b5","uuid":"268355e9-1ba9-4808-933c-d28ad05ae5d3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:03:43.619Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"**Sports (Sensible Soccer, NBA Jam, Tecmo Bowl).** Start from the SPORTS slice: two against two in a walled cage, up to four players.\n- The field is a `TileMap` cage in `threequarter` (boards that cut low before the camera, nets); the ball and the players are `E.Body`s. The ball bounces off the ground and the boards (`bounce`), and curls: turn its velocity a little across its path each step while the shooter pushes sideways (aftertouch).\n- A pass leads the teammate (aim where it is going, not where it is); a lob over a defender is `E.arc(from, to, gravity, { apex })`, the throw that lands at its feet; a shot's power fills a meter while its button is held and goes on letting go.\n- The players a person doesn't run play by formation, by where the ball is: with it, the other one runs ahead on the far side; without it, the nearer presses and the other covers the goal. `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })` lets players 2 to 4 in, each taking a side's next player.\n\n**First-person dungeon (Wizardry, Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder).** The 3D CRAWLER kit (the grid module). The 3D engine's `'fixed'` camera at the party's eyes over a level of 2 x 2 tiles a cell; each step and quarter turn is a tween, so the view glides. Gates are `world.thing('door')`s that rise (`world.unlock` for one with a key); the monsters walk an `E.Grid` cell to cell; `E.Fog` keeps what the party has seen for the automap; `E.Turns` in `'atb'` is real time (Dungeon Master), in `'speed'` the dungeon waits for the party (Wizardry). The party's portraits sit under the view (`rig.drawPortrait`).\n\n**Twin-stick shooter (Robotron 2084, Smash TV).** Start from the ADVENTURE kit (a `Body` hero in rooms) with the SHOOTER's ships and bullets.\n- One fixed room in `topdown` (`res: [320, 240]`, `expand`): the hero a `Body` moved by `input.move()`, the left stick or WASD; it fires the way the right stick points (`input.padAim`), else toward the mouse (`input.pointer()` to a ground point), else the way it moves, a shot every 0.08 s from an `E.Bullets` pool (`plane: 'ground'`).\n- Waves spawn from the room's edges by a timeline; grunts walk straight at the hero, others wander, hulks can't be killed, humans to rescue for points. `cam.shake` and `game.freeze(.03)` on every kill keep it loud; `E.Arcade` keeps the score, the lives and the table.\n\n**Bomberman.** Start from the PUZZLE slice's grid or the ARCADE's maze (the grid module).\n- The arena is an `E.Grid` of hard blocks on even cells and soft blocks to break; players and foes are `E.GridMover`s (a turn asked early is kept).\n\n41: *    interface (title, pause, settings, help, results, map screens and a HUD with a minimap) from data: new E.Shell(game,\n1263:const PAD_GLYPHS = {\n1304:const GLYPHS = {\n1322:const G57 = {\n2357:    /** the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null */\n2500:  menu(name) {\n2530:    if (this.o.menu !== false) new Shell(this, { system: true });\n2973: *    E.Shell draws the menu's screens (pause, settings, controls): section 21d.\n2999:  glyphs: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['xbox', 'Xbox'], ['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['nintendo', 'Nintendo'], ['generic', 'Positions']], apply: (g, v) => { g.input.glyphs = v; } },\n3031:    /** onChange(key, value): called after every change (E.Shell's settings.onChange goes through it) */\n3877:  /** open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or\n4347:    if (this.o.style === 'classic') this._drawClassic(g, ox, oy, view); else this._drawHD(g, ox, oy, view);\n4353:  _drawHD(g, ox, oy, view) {\n4479:        if (o.hat) this._hat(g, Sp, J, r, H);\n4501:      if (o.hat) this._hat(g, Sp, J, r, H);\n4604:        if (o.hat) this._hat(g, Sp, J, r, H);\n4637:  _hat(g, Sp, J, r, H) {\n4645:    } else if (st === 'helmet') {  // robot / knight helmet that leaves the face open\n8956:    if (this.voice && Math.floor(this.shown) > prev && (this._blip++ % 2 === 0)) this.game.audio.sfx(this.voice);\n9091: *      const ui = new E.Shell(game, { theme: { accent: '#d9b77c' }, settings: { items: ['sound', 'volume', 'motion'] },\n9103: *    THE STANDARD MENU: every game gets one (new E.Game makes this shell for itself, and a game's own E.Shell takes over\n9109: *    false }, quit: 'title' } }) adjusts it; menu: false, or new E.Shell(game, { standard: false }), leaves it out.\n9163:class Shell {\n9165:   * new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings',\n9373:  _settingsRows(add) {\n9460:    if (name === 'settings') this._settingsRows(add);\n9585:E.Shell = Shell;\n13389:  /** the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save\n14126:- rts.fog (E.Fog: the player's sight; walls block it), rts.visible(u); rts.minimap() is E.Shell's hud({ minimap }) (the\n14399:  /** E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera */","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0156nNt5Ae9qmigUxt4apZ6H","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
