{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lan2GrVhB1eASQztXbhaJs","type":"tool_result","content":"366:- `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity = 1, o)` †: radius in world units; intensity ~0.5..1.5. opts: { color: '#ffaa55' (both lightings), shadow: true (GPU lighting: walls and casters block it) }\n367:- `game.lights.caster(x, y, r, top)` †: something that blocks light (GPU shadows): a cylinder of radius r from the floor up to height top\n368:- `game.lights.heat(x, y, z, width, strength = 1)` †: heat shimmer above a point (GPU only). width in world units, strength ~0.5..1.5\n369:- `game.lights.on` †: true when the canvas lighting draws this frame: enabled, or standing in for GPU lighting the game turned on that can't draw (no WebGPU, still loading, a side view); gpu.fallback = false keeps such a frame\n370:- `game.lights.refresh()` †: rebuild the darkness bands after changing dark, levels or glow (lights.dark = [r, g, b]; lights.refresh())\n371:- `game.lights.render(r)` †: darken the frame by the lights (the renderer calls it after the queue, when enabled)\n372:- `game.lights.ambient = .15` †: how lit unlit places are, 0 (black) .. 1\n373:- `game.lights.dark = [10, 6, 24]` †: the color of darkness, [r, g, b]\n374:- `game.lights.darkness = .9` †: how dark the darkest places get, 0..1 (the smooth style, E.style.trans 'alpha')\n375:- `game.lights.enabled = false` †: false (the default) turns the canvas lighting off\n376:- `game.lights.glow = [255, 200, 140, 0]` †: the color, [r, g, b, a], where light is brightest\n377:- `game.lights.glowAt = 1.7` †: the light level (1 = fully lit) above which it glows\n378:- `game.lights.levels = [.9, .7, .48, .26, .08, 0]` †: the darkness of each lighting band, darkest first (dithered between them)\n379:- `game.lights.list = []` †: this frame's lights from add()\n380:- `game.lights.screen = false` †: true measures lights on the screen, not the ground (side views and PlatformMaps do it by themselves)\n381:- `game.lights.tint = .32` †: how strongly lights add their own color, 0..1\n427:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also\n475:- `game.enableGPU(o = {})` †: turn on WebGPU lighting: where it can't draw (no WebGPU, a side view) the canvas lighting stands in, with its own ambient (game.lights.ambient) and the same lights. opts: { map, bands, ambient, fa\n1198:- `game.gpu.enabled = true` †: false switches it off for now (and the canvas lighting with it, unless game.lights.enabled)\n1200:- `game.gpu.fallback = true` †: false keeps a frame it can't draw unlit (by default the canvas lighting stands in, game.lights.on)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1931e3d-b97b-4f9d-8b9d-c7660f7740b5","uuid":"36d3d7bd-fd7e-40b1-ac06-8312c77ab63e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:15:06.047Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"366:- `game.lights.add(x, y, z, radius, intensity = 1, o)` †: radius in world units; intensity ~0.5..1.5. opts: { color: '#ffaa55' (both lightings), shadow: true (GPU lighting: walls and casters block it) }\n367:- `game.lights.caster(x, y, r, top)` †: something that blocks light (GPU shadows): a cylinder of radius r from the floor up to height top\n368:- `game.lights.heat(x, y, z, width, strength = 1)` †: heat shimmer above a point (GPU only). width in world units, strength ~0.5..1.5\n369:- `game.lights.on` †: true when the canvas lighting draws this frame: enabled, or standing in for GPU lighting the game turned on that can't draw (no WebGPU, still loading, a side view); gpu.fallback = false keeps such a frame\n370:- `game.lights.refresh()` †: rebuild the darkness bands after changing dark, levels or glow (lights.dark = [r, g, b]; lights.refresh())\n371:- `game.lights.render(r)` †: darken the frame by the lights (the renderer calls it after the queue, when enabled)\n372:- `game.lights.ambient = .15` †: how lit unlit places are, 0 (black) .. 1\n373:- `game.lights.dark = [10, 6, 24]` †: the color of darkness, [r, g, b]\n374:- `game.lights.darkness = .9` †: how dark the darkest places get, 0..1 (the smooth style, E.style.trans 'alpha')\n375:- `game.lights.enabled = false` †: false (the default) turns the canvas lighting off\n376:- `game.lights.glow = [255, 200, 140, 0]` †: the color, [r, g, b, a], where light is brightest\n377:- `game.lights.glowAt = 1.7` †: the light level (1 = fully lit) above which it glows\n378:- `game.lights.levels = [.9, .7, .48, .26, .08, 0]` †: the darkness of each lighting band, darkest first (dithered between them)\n379:- `game.lights.list = []` †: this frame's lights from add()\n380:- `game.lights.screen = false` †: true measures lights on the screen, not the ground (side views and PlatformMaps do it by themselves)\n381:- `game.lights.tint = .32` †: how strongly lights add their own color, 0..1\n427:- `r.prop(name, x, y, z, o = {})` †: set dressing from E.prop: r.prop('torch', x, y, z, { size, color, flip, light: true, halo: true, bias, hides, footprint }) feet on the world point; flames animate and glow. light: true also\n475:- `game.enableGPU(o = {})` †: turn on WebGPU lighting: where it can't draw (no WebGPU, a side view) the canvas lighting stands in, with its own ambient (game.lights.ambient) and the same lights. opts: { map, bands, ambient, fa\n1198:- `game.gpu.enabled = true` †: false switches it off for now (and the canvas lighting with it, unless game.lights.enabled)\n1200:- `game.gpu.fallback = true` †: false keeps a frame it can't draw unlit (by default the canvas lighting stands in, game.lights.on)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Lan2GrVhB1eASQztXbhaJs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
