{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user invoked `/goal` with the condition: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\" A Stop hook blocks stopping until this holds.\n   - STAGE.md: build the game TASK.md describes, following PLAN.md (title from the plan: **American Football Fiasco**); where they disagree TASK.md wins; deliver the file name and the reply sections TASK.md asks for.\n   - TASK.md key requirements: arcade over-the-top American football; single HTML `AmericanFootballFiasco-AmericanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-070229.html` in the work root; dev files in subfolder `AmericanFootballFiasco-AmericanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-070229/`; built on my-3d2dge handoff (may modify engine); native art/animation plus new; all audio in code with Animalese/Simlish voices; AI Hub multiplayer (and standalone); feature-complete demo; Dev mode from pause menu with live sliders + reset to defaults; attract mode after 10 s idle on title/menu (AI may cheat; any input exits); 10-foot controller-first UI, PS glyphs default with Settings option for Xbox, keyboard/mouse native, prompts follow last device; touch-only: \"Controller or keyboard required\" + settings button, attract still runs; no TODOs/placeholders/stubs; Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback in chat reply AND in-game About/Credits; exit-interview.json in exact shape (sourceInformation {date, source, plan, genre, perspective, tech, artDirection, animation, audio, online, testing, research, environment, model, usage}, testingFeedback[4], engineFeedback[6], promptFeedback[4], aiHub {name, tagline, description, type, genre, source, series, players, controls, tags}); write \"unknown\" for anything unconfirmable. Date: 2026-11-04 07:02:29; Environment: \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\"; Model: \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\".\n   - Security/process constraints from TASK.md (verbatim): \"Do not read files outside what you need - other agents share this directory. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\" Testing: \"Keep them behind one command that prints only failures and a one-line count, and rerun it only after changing the code it covers. Use screenshots only for what a script can't check. Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\" PLAN.md also: don't commit to git unless asked; keep caches/output in the dev folder (/tmp is small).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 engine (E.Game scenes, res 'ps1' expand, E.View custom views, TileMap floorTex bake keyed per view+scale (zoom rebakes → quantized zoom steps + world-space precomputed texture), r.actor/r.queue/r.decal/r.overlay, HD Humanoid rigs, E.MOVES/E.move, mocap (Mocap.load/drive, rig.mocap/mocapW/mocapMask), E.Shell screens/settings, game.settings.define, game.saves, E.Dialog, audio chip synth (define/sfx/music/layer/sting/tempo), particles, lights, weather, E.store over localStorage, game.advance headless).\n   - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 shared-world (session.js 1.4.0 pasted first in head; connect with card:true; ready/answer/send/finish/time/rng/on events card,start,message,leave,time-up,end).\n   - Sim/presentation split; intents per athlete; FF.bus events + modifiers (addMod/mod/tickPlays/clearMods); deterministic FF.rng.sim; PoseFX joint post-processing; Play Lab; autopilot (FF.autopilot) for tests; side-aware cheats (m.cheatSide).\n   - Tests in Node vm contexts with stand-ins; Playwright Chromium for screenshots and hub harness.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (all under the dev folder unless noted):\n   - `tools/patch-engine.mjs`: regenerates `vendor/my-3d2dge.js` from `.cache/my-3d2dge.orig.js` applying E1–E8, E10 (glyphs ✕○□△·—☆‹›; glyphs default 'playstation' options playstation/xbox + Controller row on Settings; o.gear hook in _drawHD; 'football' hat + facemask; Dialog voice fn; audio.bus/busVol; Shell `rows` + Dev groups hidden; menu(name,{pause:false}); floor cache 14).\n   - `index.html`: session.js first after meta charset, hub:* metas, e3-boot splash, all vendor and src scripts in order, `src/about.js` before `src/90-main.js`; canvas pixelated.\n   - `build.mjs`: inlines scripts (escapes `</script`), generates `src/about.js` (window.FF_ABOUT) from `src/about.json`, writes `../AmericanFootballFiasco-AmericanFootball-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-070229.html` and `../exit-interview.json` (shape {sourceInformation, testingFeedback, engineFeedback, promptFeedback, aiHub}), verifies parse and session.js SHA match. Last build: 2.01 MB, hash matches, first script in head.\n   - `src/about.json`: sourceInformation filled (date, source \"American football (over the top arcade style)\", plan \"PLAN.md\", genre, perspective, tech, artDirection, animation, audio, online, testing, research \"none beyond reading the engine handoff docs, the AI Hub README and the plan\", environment, model, usage \"unknown\"); **testingFeedback/engineFeedback/promptFeedback currently [\"unknown\",...] — must be replaced with real answers before finishing**; aiHub filled (name \"American Football Fiasco\", tagline \"Over-the-top arcade football\", type Game, genre Sports, source \"American football\", series \"\", players \"1–4\", controls, tags [arcade, comedy, versus, co-op, story, retro]); credits; engineChanges list (E1–E8, E10).\n   - src modules 00–90 as listed in analysis (game code). Notable recent edits: 31-sim-play ghostT pass-through after evasion, stiff-arm knocks tackler down, tackle reach rad+rad+7, cheatOn side-aware, catch radius +8 for target; 33-ai lane check, scrape, force edge read, catch-up boost, evasive odds lowered, freeRun forward weight 4.5; 30-sim auto-kick after T.autoHike for idle human kicker, CPU FG power uses fgDistance*1.16+2, kick meter press at min(.97,want); 36-ots heat cool-off (heatAge 5 plays); 34-ai-coach FG before go-for-it; 35-control presnap clamp uses offense dir `Do = m.dir(m.poss)`, lockCtl, remote inputOf; 52-scene-match hub client branch, countdown, end overlay, Results.layout(); 51/54/55 layouts computed in update; 56 attract AT.since guard; 50 idle pointer null→value counts.\n   - Tests: `test/run.mjs`, `test/lib/context.mjs` (localStorage stand-in, matchMedia/touch options, hub option), `test/lib/sim.mjs` (simCtx, match, until, call), suites `01-boot` … `13-story` (all passing: boot 21, data 387, rules 16, actions, ai, ots, replay, control, ui + audio-dev 74, drills 9, attract 24, story 20), `test/balance.mjs`, `test/browser/peek.mjs`, `test/browser/hub.mjs` (all 4 harness configs PASS: players=2; players=4 latency150 jitter50 loss5; host-leave; server).\n\n4. Errors and fixes (key ones):\n   - Stale intents moved athletes pre-snap → zero intents; updateMovers only in PLAYCALL/COIN/QBREAK/HALFTIME; zero intents at line set.\n   - Case-sensitive `/block/` regex never engaged blockers → `/i`; engagement push too strong → `Math.min(40, |force|*.3)`; C's snap action blocked engagement → `busy` excludes snap/shed; added `lockLines()` at snap.\n   - QB free-ran before handoff → qbNoBall until handed; counter play blocking reworked.\n   - QB passing-lane counted DL in front → count only defenders past max(6yd, 45% of lane) within 1.6yd.\n   - Sweep/toss TD machine → force edge read, catch-up pursuit boost, tighter paths, speedPerSpd 5.5; leverage rewrite that made runs worse was reverted.\n   - smoothDamp wrong signature → 5 args.\n   - dev.applyCheat used before defined → guarded.\n   - Menus' Focus items only built in draw (headless couldn't pick) → layout in update for menu, setup options, story board, fiasco, practice, results.\n   - Engine store uses localStorage (none in Node) → test context stand-in.\n   - CPU kick meter never pressed when want power 1 → min(.97).\n   - Attract input ignored at loop restart → AT.since; pointer first appearance counts as input.\n   - Drill bot failures fixed (ghost after evade; stiff-arm knockdown; presnap defender clamp direction bug teleported S into backfield; hurdle trigger 2.7yd; catching lockCtl and rep ends at catch; passing rep ends at catch; INT lesson removes OL and forces throw to receiver nearest human; defense drill tackle.p +.35 for humans; playcall drill judged on 'called' event).\n   - Lines > 48 chars shortened; missing glyphs added; audio.layer warnings guarded; python http.server output buffering → `-u`.\n   - Tests' own issues fixed (forceCall persisting after PAT, safety test made deterministic, hotWhy 'streak', replay hash checked with 1/120 steps, Results 0.6 s input guard timing).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Full scripted playthrough (title → story → prologue → nine tryout drills by bots → chapters 2–5 on autopilot with halftime choices → ending → credits; plus loss → THAT'S A FIASCO → RETRY; plus 2-player exhibition → results → REMATCH) passes.\n   - Balance (test/balance.mjs, 8 games): points 15.0/team, completion 69%, sacks 1.3, turnovers 3.5 (varies 2.0–3.5), FG 40–49 fine, live 3.2 s/play (short), hot streaks 2.5/game, fills 1.9.\n   - Hub harness passes all configs; a live 2-player round showed synced play.\n   - Visual checks done (title, menu, setup, story board, attract, drill, match, play call, night stadium); several layout fixes applied.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The `/goal` command with args: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.\"\n   - System/harness nudges (not user requests): \"The user hasn't heard from you in a while — say in a few words what you're doing, then continue.\" (several times).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Write the net suite (fake AIHub across 2–4 vm contexts with latency/loss; check traffic both ways, ≤18 msgs/s, snapshots ≤1100 bytes, finish once with valid standings, every copy ended, nothing sent after end, leave handling) — optional but planned.\n   - Browser suite: `node tools/check.mjs <deliverable> --size 1920x1080` and `1280x720`, act on look notes; deep links play without errors.\n   - Write `ENGINE-CHANGES.md` (what/where/why for E1–E8, E10; engine and hub commits 4390a9852fe0ad01e1699a160f2a331931bb1a72 / f8835e4824fbf9bbb4bac3a35e88e3ab197fdd1e).\n   - Replace \"unknown\" placeholders in `src/about.json` testingFeedback (4), engineFeedback (6), promptFeedback (4) with real answers; set usage (\"unknown\" acceptable); rebuild with `node build.mjs`; verify `../exit-interview.json` parses and every field is filled.\n   - Run the full `npm test` (and `--browser`/hub harness on the final file); ensure no TODO/placeholder strings in src.\n   - Optional polish: remaining visual tweaks; cleanup (.cache may be deleted; no servers running).\n   - Final chat reply: short game summary + Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback (same as About screen/exit interview).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Writing and running the remaining test suites. Just created `test/suites/09-ui.mjs` (menus by keys/mouse, settings specs incl. glyphs default playstation/xbox, game.menu('settings'), pause items Dev Mode/Restart, touch-only detection/attract) and `test/suites/10-audio-dev.mjs` (voice plans deterministic, every profile plans, question contour, Commentary Off, songs parse, stadium songs exist, Dev sliders change FF.T and reset, Play Lab stats, cheat toggle reaches match, every Dev page opens, JUMP TO situation, no unknown-sound warnings), and ran `timeout 900 node test/run.mjs ui audio-dev` → \"74 passed, 0 failed (0.7 s)\".\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue the remaining finishing steps in order: (1) optionally add the net suite with a fake hub; (2) run `node tools/check.mjs` on the bundle at 1920x1080 and 1280x720 and address look notes; (3) write `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`; (4) fill real Testing/Engine/Prompt feedback answers in `src/about.json` (testing caught many issues — e.g., blocking regex, presnap stale intents, menu focus in draw, drill bot/clamp bugs; critical ones like blocking never engaging, QB sacked before handoff, defender teleport), run `node build.mjs`, verify `../exit-interview.json` parses; (5) run the full `node test/run.mjs` and `node test/browser/hub.mjs` on the final file; (6) give the final reply with the four required sections. This continues directly from the last action: \"Now UI, audio and Dev suites, then the network suite over a fake hub with simulated latency and loss.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /h