{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiAeo5Vu5dDk2w832vfa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":541,"cache_read_input_tokens":97499,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":541},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1931e3d-b97b-4f9d-8b9d-c7660f7740b5","uuid":"fb82bb33-8476-4b24-8af0-7fda3e32a9ee","timestamp":"2026-11-04T16:00:52.221Z","request_id":"req_011CgiAenqN1XLev3HjZbcEV","thinking_duration_ms":2551,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiAeo5Vu5dDk2w832vfa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The pick-six fires again. Now the feedback answers in `about.json`; after that, one full test run and a rebuild."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":541,"cache_read_input_tokens":97499,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":541},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1931e3d-b97b-4f9d-8b9d-c7660f7740b5","uuid":"51b1329e-cc94-4dc7-a5ad-ade6e9471f31","timestamp":"2026-11-04T16:00:52.222Z","request_id":"req_011CgiAenqN1XLev3HjZbcEV"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiAeo5Vu5dDk2w832vfa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GdU2tiN5HRz1YusW81xNbi","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='src/about.json'; d=json.load(open(p))\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n \"About 30 game issues, plus 5 mistakes in the tests themselves. The headless suites, scripted playthroughs and bot-played drills found most. Screenshots found the rest: layout overlaps, text over 48 characters, missing font glyphs, and a night cutscene lit like noon.\",\n \"6 game breaking: blockers never engaged (a case-sensitive /block/ check), the QB ran off before the handoff and got sacked, a pre-snap clamp teleported the safety into the backfield, a CPU kicker that never pressed the meter stalled the kickoff, opening a Dev cheat threw an error, and stale run intents moved players before the snap.\",\n \"The bot-played tryout drills and the full story run: bots press the real inputs through every drill, then the story is autopiloted chapter by chapter to the credits. That one run found the defender teleport, the stiff-arm and hurdle bugs, and the menus that could only be picked once drawn.\",\n \"The replay determinism check. Its only failure was a mistake in the test itself (the wrong step size), never a bug in the game.\"]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n \"game.advance with no screen: the whole game (matches, drills, story, attract, a four-copy hub session) runs in Node, so the tests are fast and deterministic. Close behind: the HD Humanoid rigs with E.MOVES and mocap, and the Shell giving pause, settings and controls screens for free.\",\n \"Yes. The TileMap floor bake is cached per view and scale, so a smoothly zooming broadcast camera re-baked the field every frame until I quantized the zoom and raised the cache size (E10). I also guessed smoothDamp's arguments wrong, missed that E.store needs localStorage (absent in Node), and built menu focus lists in draw, which headless runs never call.\",\n \"The football itself: an athlete simulation with per-athlete intents, line blocking and shedding, routes and coverage, pass flight with catch, deflection and interception odds, tackling with pursuit angles, the rules (downs, clock, penalties, scoring) and the coach AI. Close second: shared-world netcode with client prediction on top of the hub's session.js.\",\n \"Keeping 22 HD rigs, the crowd and a baked field at a steady frame rate with a camera that zooms and pans, and learning which systems are tied to draw (focus lists, light refresh, floor bakes) so the headless runs behave like the browser.\",\n \"E1 PlayStation glyphs in both pixel fonts; E2 glyphs default to PlayStation with Xbox in Settings; E3 a gear hook in the HD rig's depth sort (pads, facemasks, numbers, the ball); E4 a football helmet hat; E5 a Dialog voice callback for Animalese; E6 audio buses for voices and crowd; E7 setting rows on any Shell screen, Dev groups hidden; E8 open Settings without pausing a shared world; E10 keep 14 baked floors, not 6. The 10-foot UI is a game stylesheet. Details in ENGINE-CHANGES.md.\",\n \"Bake the floor once in world space and scale it at draw time, so the camera zoom never invalidates the cache.\"]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n \"How concrete it was. The plan names every play, card, chapter and engine change with where to find it, and the testing rule (one command, failures and a count only) kept the loop short.\",\n \"Where TASK.md and PLAN.md overlap but differ (the reply sections, the 10-foot theme as an engine change or a stylesheet), which items in a 2,400-line plan are must-haves versus nice-to-haves, and the Usage field, since no cost or token figures are visible from inside the session.\",\n \"Making the football play right: blocking, run lanes, pursuit and pass coverage balanced so runs, passes, sacks and turnovers all happen at sensible rates. Close behind: a shared-world session that stays in sync under latency and loss.\",\n \"Split the plan into priority tiers (core loop first, then modes, then polish), say outright that a fake hub in Node is an acceptable stand-in for the harness, and either drop the Usage field or say where to read the figures.\"]\nfor k in ['testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback']:\n    for v in d[k]: assert v and v!='unknown'\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); print('ok', [len(d[k]) for k in ['testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback']])\nEOF","description":"Fill the feedback answers in about.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":541,"cache_read_input_tokens":97499,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":541},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1931e3d-b97b-4f9d-8b9d-c7660f7740b5","uuid":"ab0ace90-9ec9-429b-a246-1149cc96cf04","timestamp":"2026-11-04T16:01:08.378Z","request_id":"req_011CgiAenqN1XLev3HjZbcEV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GdU2tiN5HRz1YusW81xNbi":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='src/about.json'; d=json.load(open(p))\nd['testingFeedback']=[\n \"About 30 game issues, plus 5 mistakes in the tests themselves. The headless suites, scripted playthroughs and bot-played drills found most. Screenshots found the rest: layout overlaps, text over 48 characters, missing font glyphs, and a night cutscene lit like noon.\",\n \"6 game breaking: blockers never engaged (a case-sensitive /block/ check), the QB ran off before the handoff and got sacked, a pre-snap clamp teleported the safety into the backfield, a CPU kicker that never pressed the meter stalled the kickoff, opening a Dev cheat threw an error, and stale run intents moved players before the snap.\",\n \"The bot-played tryout drills and the full story run: bots press the real inputs through every drill, then the story is autopiloted chapter by chapter to the credits. That one run found the defender teleport, the stiff-arm and hurdle bugs, and the menus that could only be picked once drawn.\",\n \"The replay determinism check. Its only failure was a mistake in the test itself (the wrong step size), never a bug in the game.\"]\nd['engineFeedback']=[\n \"game.advance with no screen: the whole game (matches, drills, story, attract, a four-copy hub session) runs in Node, so the tests are fast and deterministic. Close behind: the HD Humanoid rigs with E.MOVES and mocap, and the Shell giving pause, settings and controls screens for free.\",\n \"Yes. The TileMap floor bake is cached per view and scale, so a smoothly zooming broadcast camera re-baked the field every frame until I quantized the zoom and raised the cache size (E10). I also guessed smoothDamp's arguments wrong, missed that E.store needs localStorage (absent in Node), and built menu focus lists in draw, which headless runs never call.\",\n \"The football itself: an athlete simulation with per-athlete intents, line blocking and shedding, routes and coverage, pass flight with catch, deflection and interception odds, tackling with pursuit angles, the rules (downs, clock, penalties, scoring) and the coach AI. Close second: shared-world netcode with client prediction on top of the hub's session.js.\",\n \"Keeping 22 HD rigs, the crowd and a baked field at a steady frame rate with a camera that zooms and pans, and learning which systems are tied to draw (focus lists, light refresh, floor bakes) so the headless runs behave like the browser.\",\n \"E1 PlayStation glyphs in both pixel fonts; E2 glyphs default to PlayStation with Xbox in Settings; E3 a gear hook in the HD rig's depth sort (pads, facemasks, numbers, the ball); E4 a football helmet hat; E5 a Dialog voice callback for Animalese; E6 audio buses for voices and crowd; E7 setting rows on any Shell screen, Dev groups hidden; E8 open Settings without pausing a shared world; E10 keep 14 baked floors, not 6. The 10-foot UI is a game stylesheet. Details in ENGINE-CHANGES.md.\",\n \"Bake the floor once in world space and scale it at draw time, so the camera zoom never invalidates the cache.\"]\nd['promptFeedback']=[\n \"How concrete it was. The plan names every play, card, chapter and engine change with where to find it, and the testing rule (one command, failures and a count only) kept the loop short.\",\n \"Where TASK.md and PLAN.md overlap but differ (the reply sections, the 10-foot theme as an engine change or a stylesheet), which items in a 2,400-line plan are must-haves versus nice-to-haves, and the Usage field, since no cost or token figures are visible from inside the session.\",\n \"Making the football play right: blocking, run lanes, pursuit and pass coverage balanced so runs, passes, sacks and turnovers all happen at sensible rates. Close behind: a shared-world session that stays in sync under latency and loss.\",\n \"Split the plan into priority tiers (core loop first, then modes, then polish), say outright that a fake hub in Node is an acceptable stand-in for the harness, and either drop the Usage field or say where to read the figures.\"]\nfor k in ['testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback']:\n    for v in d[k]: assert v and v!='unknown'\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); print('ok', [len(d[k]) for k in ['testingFeedback','engineFeedback','promptFeedback']])\nEOF","description":"Fill the feedback answers in about.json"}}}
